descendants of Tsephon","p":"tsef-o-nee'","t":"tsephoni","g":"the Zephonite[s]","fb":[["zephonites","Zephonites","Man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness","Gad's clan through Zephon, counted in the Numbers 26 census.","person",1]],"v":[4504]},"H6856":{"l":"צִפֹּרֶן","x":"tsippôren","d":"properly, a claw, i.e. (human) nail; also the point of a style (or pen, tipped with adamant)","p":"tsip-po'-ren","t":"tsipporen","g":"nails","fb":[],"v":[5459,19357]},"H6891":{"l":"צָרְתָן","x":"Tsârᵉthân","d":"Tsarethan, a place in Palestine","p":"tsaw-reth-awn'","t":"tsarethan","g":"Zarethan","fb":[["zarthan","Zarthan","Zarethan","The Jordan's waters piled up near Zarthan when Israel crossed on dry ground. Centuries later Solomon's bronze for the temple was cast in the clay ground between Succoth and Zarthan. Exactly where in the plain it stood is uncertain.","place",3]],"v":[5909,8856,8980]},"H6890":{"l":"צֶרֶת הַשַּׁחַר","x":"Tsereth hash-Shachar","d":"Tsereth-hash-Shachar, a place in Palestine","p":"tseh'-reth hash-shakh'-ar","t":"tsereth hash-shachar","g":"Zereth","fb":[["zareth-shahar","Zareth-shahar","Zereth-shahar","Splendor of the dawn. It was a town of Reuben on a hill above the plain by the Dead Sea, usually placed near the mouth of the Wadi Zarqa Ma'in.","place",1]],"v":[6173,6173]},"H6829":{"l":"צָפוֹן","x":"Tsâphôwn","d":"Tsaphon, a place in Palestine","p":"tsaw-fone'","t":"tsaphon","g":"Zaphon","fb":[["zaphon","Zaphon","","The name means north, and it was a town of Gad in the Jordan Valley. Some scholars find it again in Judges 12:1, where the Ephraimites gather to confront Jephthah. Nobody has located it.","place",1]],"v":[6181]},"H6860":{"l":"צִקְלַג","x":"Tsiqlag","d":"Tsiklag or Tsikelag, a place in Palestine","p":"tsik-lag'","t":"tsiqlag","g":"Ziklag","fb":[["ziklag","Ziklag","","Achish of Gath gave this town in the Negev to David while he was running from Saul, and David lived there more than a year. Amalekites burned it while he was away and took the women and children, and he went after them and got everyone back.","place",12]],"v":[6233,6326,7936,7936,7979,7979,7979,7992,8004,8023,8130,10415,10720,10740,12615]},"H6881":{"l":"צׇרְעָה","x":"Tsorʻâh","d":"Tsorah, a place in Palestine","p":"tsor-aw'","t":"tsorah","g":"Zorah","fb":[["zareah","Zareah","Zorah","Samson's hometown, better known as Zorah, on the border of Judah and Dan. The angel of the Lord told Manoah's wife there that she would have a son, and Samson was buried between Zorah and Eshtaol.","place",10]],"v":[6235,6362,6886,6909,6980,6995,7001,7004,11424,12616]},"H6865":{"l":"צֹר","x":"Tsôr","d":"Tsor, a place in Palestine","p":"tsore","t":"tsor","g":"of Tyre","fb":[["tyre","Tyre","","The leading Phoenician port, partly on the mainland and partly on an island offshore, rich from sea trade and purple dye made from murex shells. Its king Hiram sent cedar and craftsmen for David and Solomon. The prophets attacked its pride and said it would fall.","place",50]],"v":[6350,8143,8699,8879,8947,9062,9063,10775,11214,11222,14608,15247,15304,18077,18081,18084,18091,18091,18093,19555,19598,20076,21101,21102,21103,21106,21114,21122,21123,21123,21128,21152,21158,21168,21200,21200,22220,22346,22372,22373,23000,23001]},"H6815":{"l":"צַעֲנַנִּים","x":"Tsaʻănannîym","d":"Tsaanannim or Tsaanajim, a place in Palestine","p":"tsah-an-an-neem'","t":"tsaanannim","g":"Zaanannim","fb":[["zaannannim","Zaannannim","Zaanannim","On Naphtali's border, near Kedesh, by the oak where Heber the Kenite had his tent. Sisera ran there after his army broke at the Kishon, and Heber's wife Jael killed him.","place",2]],"v":[6354,6610]},"H6863":{"l":"צֵר","x":"Tsêr","d":"Tser, a place in Palestine","p":"tsare","t":"tser","g":"Zer","fb":[["zer","Zer","","It was a walled town of Naphtali, probably near the southwest shore of the Sea of Galilee, exact site unknown.","place",1]],"v":[6356]},"H6857":{"l":"צְפַת","x":"Tsᵉphath","d":"Tsephath, a place in Palestine","p":"tsef-ath'","t":"tsephath","g":"Zephath","fb":[["zephath","Zephath","","Judah and Simeon took this Canaanite town, destroyed it, and renamed it Hormah. It had beaten back an Israelite attack years earlier in the wilderness. After that the old name drops out.","place",1]],"v":[6526]},"H6852":{"l":"צָפַר","x":"tsâphar","d":"to skip about, i.e. return","p":"tsaw-far'","t":"tsaphar","g":"let him go","fb":[],"v":[6697]},"H6884":{"l":"צָרַף","x":"tsâraph","d":"to fuse (metal), i.e. refine (literally or figuratively)","p":"tsaw-raf'","t":"tsaraph","g":"[is] refined","fb":[],"v":[6698,6984,8633,12335,12359,14071,14105,14147,14274,14882,14882,15624,16037,17116,17255,17678,18438,18438,18457,18591,18623,19117,19117,19181,19209,19214,20228,22070,22090,23067,23067,23121,23122]},"H6888":{"l":"צְרֵרָה","x":"Tsᵉrêrâh","d":"Tsererah for Tseredah","p":"tser-ay-raw'","t":"tsererah","g":"towards","fb":[["zererath","Zererath","Zarethan","The Midianites ran toward it when Gideon routed them, down the Jordan valley toward Beth-shittah and Abel-meholah, and the site is unknown.","place",1]],"v":[6716]},"H6877":{"l":"צְרִיחַ","x":"tsᵉrîyach","d":"a citadel","p":"tser-ee'-akh","t":"tseriach","g":"chamber","fb":[],"v":[6800,6803,6803,7491]},"H6870":{"l":"צְרוּיָה","x":"Tsᵉrûwyâh","d":"Tserujah, an Israelitess","p":"tser-oo-yaw'","t":"tseruyah","g":"of Zeruiah","fb":[["zeruiah","Zeruiah","Woman living at the time of United Monarchy","David's sister, the mother of Joab, Abishai and Asahel. David said the sons of Zeruiah were too much for him.","person",25]],"v":[7911,8062,8067,8120,8225,8357,8435,8436,8474,8480,8532,8533,8597,8671,8690,8724,8775,8792,10322,10322,10679,10712,10902,10905,11105,11133]},"H6835":{"l":"צַפַּחַת","x":"tsappachath","d":"a saucer (as flat)","p":"tsap-pakh'-ath","t":"tsappachath","g":"the jug","fb":[],"v":[7916,7917,7921,9329,9331,9333,9393]},"H6807":{"l":"צְעָדָה","x":"tsᵉʻâdâh","d":"a march; (concretely) an (ornamental) ankle-chain","p":"tseh-aw-daw'","t":"tseadah","g":"marching","fb":[],"v":[8156,1078